Blocking #108; #108 blocked_by #107; #118 blocked_by #109/#111/#115/#116/#117. Related links to #78 present on all three AC issues. 'crosslink issue ready' confirms functional triage: #106 listed (first phase), #107/#108/#118 absent (blocked). The 'ready' gate correctly prevents early Wave 3 launch.\n\n(4) #110 Root-cause record — VERIFIED + LIVE-REPRODUCED. The CORRECTION result comment on #78 (00:11) reads exactly as claimed (sandbox permission-enforcement defect; misattribution to model capability amended). This session reproduced the defect first-hand: git status / git log / ls / cat all DENIED despite the effective permission rules declaring 'git *' / 'ls *' / 'cat *' ALLOWED; only 'crosslink *' executes. Matches #109 and the amended record precisely.\n\n### MUST FIX (blocking)\n- None.\n\n### SHOULD CONSIDER (non-blocking)\n- #113 result comment states 'closed 56 stale test artifacts' but the audit trail (closed_at timestamps) and the stated ranges (#6-#11, #28-#43, #47-#48, #50-#71, #79-#98 = 6+16+2+22+20 = 66) show 66 issues were closed in the wave window, and the comment's own 'reduced to 32 (from ~98)' arithmetic only reconciles with 66 (98-66=32; 98-56=42). The closures themselves are correct; the '56' figure in the record is a miscount. Recommend correcting the comment to 66 (65 stale test artifacts + #87 real work) for record accuracy.\n- #113 comment says 'kept #87' but #87 IS closed (closed_at 2026-08-01T00:53:26, mid-wave) — the follow-on phrase 'closed as completed since deliverable exists' is the accurate one. Closure is defensible (agent definitions verified present), but the wording is self-contradictory and should be tightened.\n- #112: the auto_steal=false decision is right, but the empirical [STALE] flag on a minutes-old active lock should be recorded as explicit evidence in the Wave-1 hook-deployment step (#109) so the auto_steal flip is not made before heartbeat hooks land.\n\n### NITS\n- None material.\n\n### NOTABLE POSITIVES\n- All four Wave 0 sub-issues are genuinely complete and match their result comments; nothing was rubber-stamped.\n- #113's --no-changelog discipline held (CHANGELOG clean of 66 test-artifact entries).\n- The exclusions from Big Pickle's review were honored precisely — #73/#74, #78, #87, #106-#118, and real research all survived the bulk-close.\n- #111's process-level enforcement caveat was honestly recorded (edges are documentation, not machine-gated at launch) — correct framing for Wave 3.","created_at":"2026-08-01T01:09:19.451625381Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:xv6KV/c98SFKbfuU7/jxjbuRUVG7S8EbqZ6qxkKLaxI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgSyMUFF4q4pmIo/ulnwEdE7xUI/Rd8JcQCS4q41T/Jp4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAjaoQmkSN4LBWEv4WqpLIpKfPZweAqsDnA9K5NsnX45JPDbveS6DaXBAPTjOAPSjnEE2vJ4pwUHugPyfWVCddAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:xv6KV/c98SFKbfuU7/jxjbuRUVG7S8EbqZ6qxkKLaxI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgSyMUFF4q4pmIo/ulnwEdE7xUI/Rd8JcQCS4q41T/Jp4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN9wOIBO2rI2/DCOLUwqPNuUS1Wn48Va7gZe/7V+NdGCe2SU+gf3gat6QhawqBzZpMRHe/6uN+66/kkOB8Uk3w4="}
